    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d57">

                <pb facs="0100" n="84" sameAs="frus:frus1948v09/pg84"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.44A15/3–1648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kyle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-03-16T18:00:00-06:00">March 16, 1948—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>144. Discussing withdrawal today of British cruiser <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sheffield</hi>, Foreign Minister told me his government still concerned by
                    presence unknown number British troops Belize which it regards as invasion
                    threat; therefore is reversing decision re reopening border pending report from
                    Guatemalan Consul at Belize.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d57-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Reiterating Department’s sincere interest as stated Deptels 99 and 101,<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d57-f2"/> I expressed earnest hope Guatemala may accept this
                    British conciliatory move as adequate assurances non-aggressive intentions and
                    make next gesture toward normality by reopening border. Muñoz Meany replied he
                    could not accept British assurances at face value, but did reassure me his
                    government would not use withdrawal cruiser for propaganda purposes and that
                    immediately upon receipt report from Consul at Belize and further conference
                    with President Arévalo<anchor n="3" xml:id="d57-f3"/> he would communicate with
                    me again.</p>
                <p>Foreseeing possibility Guatemala may attempt use presence British troops at
                    Belize as pretext keep alive issue, I suggest advisability Department discussing
                    situation with Ambassador Gonzalez Arévalo.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d57-f4"/> Can
                    Department inform Embassy for communication Foreign Minister if British troops
                    now in Belize represent only normal peacetime garrison.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d57-f5"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kyle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d57-f1" n="1" xml:id="d57-f1-content">
                <p>Ambassador Kyle reported in telegram 150, March 19, 4 p. m., not printed, that
                    the Foreign Minister had said closure of the border with British Honduras and
                    other restrictions would be maintained until all doubt of British hostility or
                    intimidation were removed (714.44A15/3–1948).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d57-f2" n="2" xml:id="d57-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 101, March 15, 6 p. m. not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d57-f3" n="3" xml:id="d57-f3-content">
                <p>Juan José Arévalo, Guatemalan President.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d57-f4" n="4" xml:id="d57-f4-content">
                <p>Ismael Gonzalez Arévalo, Guatemalan Ambassador in the United States. He presented
                    his credentials on March 15.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d57-f5" n="5" xml:id="d57-f5-content">
                <p>In telegram 106, March 17, 6 p. m., Secretary Marshall instructed Ambassador Kyle
                    as follows: “British Emb this morning informed Dept that British Govt considers
                    its troops in Belize not in excess of normal peace-time garrison (urtel 144,
                    March 16). You may so inform FonMin.” (714.44A15/1648)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
